An electric kettle is a necessity for every family, but after a long period of use, it tends to accumulate scale, which not only affects the beauty of the kettle, but also influences the water quality. Therefore, it is critical to remove the scale.
Cut the lemon into slices, put it in the electric kettle, and pour water to make it immersed, then the scale in the kettle will naturally fall off after the water is boiling. In this way, the limescale will be removed, and there will be the fragrance of lemon in the kettle.
The specific steps: first prepare a basin of cold water, and connect the empty kettle to the power supply to dry boiling, and cut off the power when you hear a violent sound in the kettle. After that, pour cold water into the pot, and then repeat this process about 3-5 times, so that the scale will fall off by itself.
Using baking soda Put the baking soda powder into the electric kettle without heating it, and put a little water in it, soak it for one night, and the scale on the electric kettle can be removed.
Put eggs or eggshells in the electric kettle, then pour water into it, and let it boil. You can do this several times, so that the scale on the electric kettle will fall off and the water you drink will also have no peculiar smell.
