In mechanical recycling, waste plastics are shredded and melted to make recycled materials, which are then used to produce new products.
Another reason is that plastic waste usually consists of a mixture of different plastic types that cannot be separated from each other.
BASF researchers specifically solve these problems by developing various plastic additive packages to stabilize and improve the quality of recycled materials.
Chemical recycling, for example through a thermochemical process called pyrolysis, converts plastic waste into secondary raw materials.
The advantage of this method is that it can also recover mixed and unclean plastic waste streams.
This means that for the first time this kind of plastic waste can be used to make car parts, medical equipment and even food packaging.
