Wastefront is developing a waste tire recycling project in Sunderland, UK, to produce low-carbon marine and road transportation fuels and recycled carbon black (rCB).
The Norwegian recycler announced on November 25 that the two companies have been cooperating since 2019, and the new agreement will make Devaltec a “main strategic partner” of Wastefront.
The company stated: “Devaltec has signed a contract and successfully delivered a plant with a daily output of at least 1,000 MTD (tons per day) from a number of waste plants. This is the first waste tire recycling plant in Sunderland, Northeast England.
He added that Devaltec’s industry background and project experience will play a key role in realizing the potential of Wastefront.
