On merchant's website: UPOP added on merchant's website as a payment method, when cardholders check out and select to pay with UnionPay, there are two interfaces:
ExpressPay: Cardholders will be able to directly input all their UnionPay Credit Card details on merchants' websites to process payment. (only UnionPay Credit Card will be accepted through this payment channel)
WAP on the mobile: Cardholders will be directed to the UPOP official website on their phone where they can log in to their account through inputting debit cards/ credit card details to authorize the payment. Once the payment is successfully made, the link will be redirected to the merchant's website and the merchant will be notified of the transaction.
Merchant-Present: Merchants can have a static QR code printed on their cashier for cardholders' easy access or create a QR code for each payment. Merchants can simply type in the payment amount on the devices, then cardholders open their e-wallet app with a linked UnionPay credit or debit card on their phone to scan the merchant's QR code to proceed and finalized the payment.
