View Sheen's bi-spectrum series products have a high degree of integration. The thermal camera and visible light camera use the same encoder scheme, so both cameras have a unified operating interface and are easy to manage.
When people mention starlight block cameras, they tend to think of the performance of 2MP starlight block cameras. But with the promotion and popularity of AI applications, the shortcomings of 2MP starlight cameras are becoming more and more apparent in many application scenarios.,
In the same field of view, a 4MP resolution renders more image detail compared to a 2MP resolution. The 4MP resolution serves as the base resolution for edge perception, making it easier to extract critical details for the massive amount of video data structured application to lay the foundation.
The human body and face contain a large amount of feature data, but 2MP cameras are constrained by pixels and are unable to fully capture these feature data. Also, the size of a 2MP starlight sensor is 1/2 inch, while a 4MP sensor is 1/1.8 inch.
Despite the shortcomings of the 2MP starlight camera, there has not been a higher resolution camera released to the market that can match its low-light performance due to technical bottlenecks.
