The maximum tensile strength of materials used for high-strength bolts has a great relationship with quenching treatment. Generally, it is difficult to meet the material requirements of class 10.9s high-strength bolts after 40Cr quenching treatment.In addition to the different properties in the treatment process, the delayed fracture properties of high-strength bolts with different materials under high stress are also different.
The 40Cr high-strength bolt is mainly used in the bolt ball node network frame, and its design strength is generally 390MPa(d>=30mm) or 430MPa (d <30mm), without high pre-tensile stress in use.Attention should be paid to understanding and ensuring the delayed fracture performance when applying high pretension.The delayed fracture performance of 20MnTiB high strength bolt is better than that of 40B.
According to GB/ t1231-91, the recommended materials of 10.9S bolt are 20MnTiB (applicable specification <=M24) and 35VB(applicable specification <=M30).In quenching, large-diameter high-strength bolts are not easy to be fully quenched, so generally do not use large-diameter high-strength bolts, if you want to use, you should reduce its working stress.
